1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
同样叫"烧卖"，南北差一整个馅
Same name, a whole different filling

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,400
北方的，塞的是糯米饭
Up north, it's packed with sticky rice

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,600
广东的，塞猪肉和整只虾
In Canton, it's pork and whole shrimp

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,800
顶上一点橙红：蟹籽
Crowned with orange crab roe

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,000
黄色薄皮，像顶小帽子
Thin yellow skin, like a little hat

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
广东人叫它"干蒸"
Cantonese call it "gon-zing"

7
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,400
腰要捏出来，顶不封口
Pinched at the waist, left open on top

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,600
露出馅料，才够诚意
Filling on show — that's the honesty

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,800
配一盅普洱，慢慢叹一个早晨
With pu'er tea, a slow morning

10
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,000
早茶"四大天王"第二位
The second of dim sum's Four Kings

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,200
烧卖，你要广式还是北方？
Siu mai — Cantonese or northern?

12
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,600
下集：一个"会笑"的包子
Next: a bun that learns to smile
